---
// /privacy/ — Privacy Policy
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-10-01';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | YT Playlist Cal"
  description="YT Playlist Cal privacy policy — how we handle your data, what we collect, and how we protect your privacy when you use our YouTube playlist calculator."
  noindex={false}
>
  <Header />
  <main class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-8">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs" style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">
          <li><a href="/" style="color: var(--color-text-muted); text-decoration: none;">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true">›</li>
          <li aria-current="page" style="color: var(--color-text);">Privacy Policy</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text); letter-spacing: -0.03em;">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm mb-8" style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose-content space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">

        <p>
          YT Playlist Cal ("we", "our", "the tool") is an independent utility website that calculates YouTube playlist lengths and watch times. This Privacy Policy explains what information we process when you use the tool, how it is used, and how we protect your privacy.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">1. Information We Process</h2>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1 mt-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">YouTube URLs</h3>
          <p>When you submit a YouTube URL for calculation, that URL is sent to our server, which uses it to make a request to the YouTube Data API v3. <strong style="color: var(--color-text);">We do not store, log, or retain your YouTube URLs beyond the duration of the API request.</strong></p>

          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1 mt-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">YouTube API Keys (Optional)</h3>
          <p>If you provide your own YouTube API key in the Advanced Options section, it is transmitted over HTTPS and used only for your specific request. <strong style="color: var(--color-text);">We do not store, log, or transmit your API key to any third party.</strong> It is discarded after the request completes.</p>

          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1 mt-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Usage Analytics</h3>
          <p>We may use privacy-conscious analytics to understand general usage patterns such as page visits, tool usage events, and geographic distribution. This data is aggregated and not tied to individual identities. We do not send YouTube URLs or API keys to analytics services.</p>

          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1 mt-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Local Storage</h3>
          <p>We use your browser's localStorage solely to remember your dark/light mode preference. No personal data is stored in localStorage.</p>

          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1 mt-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Server Logs</h3>
          <p>Our hosting provider (Cloudflare) may maintain server access logs including IP addresses and request timestamps as part of normal server operations. These logs are governed by Cloudflare's privacy policy. We do not add additional logging of your URLs or API keys.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">2. Cookies</h2>
          <p>YT Playlist Cal does not set cookies for tracking or advertising purposes. We use no third-party tracking cookies. If you consent to analytics, a minimal analytics script may be loaded that follows privacy-by-default principles.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">3. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p><strong style="color: var(--color-text);">YouTube Data API v3:</strong> We use the YouTube Data API to retrieve playlist and video metadata. Your request goes through our server — we do not expose our API key to the client. YouTube's data use is governed by Google's Privacy Policy.</p>
          <p class="mt-2"><strong style="color: var(--color-text);">Cloudflare:</strong> Our website is hosted and proxied through Cloudflare, which may process request metadata as part of its global CDN and security services.</p>
          <p class="mt-2"><strong style="color: var(--color-text);">Font loading:</strong> We use Bunny Fonts (a GDPR-compliant alternative to Google Fonts) to load the Inter typeface. No personal data is sent to Bunny Fonts.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">4. Advertising</h2>
          <p>The website may display advertisements via Google AdSense or a comparable advertising network. Ad networks may set cookies and track behavior across websites. You can opt out of personalized advertising through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: var(--color-text);">Google Ad Settings</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">5. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>YT Playlist Cal is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">6. Your Rights</h2>
          <p>Since we do not collect or store personal data beyond transient request processing, there is typically no data to access, correct, or delete. If you have a question about data we may hold, please contact us via the Contact page.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be reflected with an updated "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of the tool after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--color-text);">8. Contact</h2>
          <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please use the <a href="/contact/" style="color: var(--color-text);">Contact page</a>.</p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
